{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Howl, inhabitants of the Makhtesh</b> — There was a street in Jerusalem for merchants and money-changers, and it is called Makhtesh, for all the city's streets have a name known to all the people of the city." "<b>the people of Canaan</b> — Every merchant is like Canaan in his hand, balances of deceit." "<b>and they shall be cut off</b> — cut off." "<b>bearers of silver</b> — like משא."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:14.950979111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}